  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR is part B0 of #917. It prepares the kernel and the geometry crate for the solidcore STEP path. It does not switch the import.\n\n- **Coordinate snap** (`crates/kernel/src/mesh_weld.rs`). Each coordinate snaps to a grid of 1e-3 mm when it is within 1e-9 mm of a grid point. The snap runs before the exact-bit weld. It gives +0.0, not -0.0. A triangle that the snap collapses is dropped. `sides()` refuses a mesh that the drop opened.\n- **Turn an inward solid outward** (`machining_mesh.rs`). A watertight mesh with a negative volume gets its winding reversed. The mesh keeps a note: \"the solid's faces all pointed inward (volume -X mm^3); the mesh is turned outward\".\n- **Refuse a breaking spline by name** (`crates/kernel/src/step_curve_guard.rs`). A pre-scan of the STEP exchange refuses an edge or swept spline that breaks the subdivision. The message names \"edge\" or \"swept\" and \"subdivision\".\n- **Adaptive refinement with a cap** (`mesh_deviation.rs`). `measure_within` refines to depth 12, with a budget of 1<<21 samples. The bound `dmax + longest 3D side` is a rigorous upper bound (the distance to a set is 1-Lipschitz, and a mesh triangle is flat). `measure` keeps depth 3. The analytic distance moved to `mesh_distance.rs` to keep the file under 400 lines.\n- **Solid ranges in the mesh** (`crates/geometry`). `Mesh.solids` holds one facet range for each solid. An empty list means one soup. `Mesh::from_solids` validates the ranges. `slice::slice_of` slices the full mesh first. On a non-manifold result with two or more ranges, it slices each range and unites the results. An inward range keeps the refusal. A range out of bounds gives `SliceError::Invalid`.\n- Eight app tests use `Mesh::from_facets` instead of a struct literal, because `Mesh` has a new field.\n\nThe decision file is `docs/decisions/917-kernel-parity.md`.\n\n## Changed pins\n\n| Test | Old | New | Cause |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `machining_mesh` Solidcraft at 0.005 | replan: yes | replan: no (largest 0.0049999913) | the adaptive bound proves the first plan |\n| `machining_mesh` Solidcraft at 0.1 | `largest() > 0.1`, replan: yes | `parametric > 0.1 && largest() <= 0.1`, replan: no (largest 0.0999999405) | the same |\n| fillet_corner at 0.005 | refused | passes (largest 0.0049998025) | the same |\n\nAll other asserts stay. No tracked fixture replans now (checked: bspline_dome, spline_revolved, bar_cross_holes, fig8, twisted_flank, sample_ap214, Milling-test, modular_clamp_unit, Solidcraft from 0.002 to 0.2).\n\n## Deviation\n\nThe snap pins are in `crates/kernel/tests/machining_mesh_parity.rs`, not in `crates/geometry/tests`. `geometry::step` is not on main, and a geometry-to-kernel edge would be necessary. The decision file records this.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/kernel/tests/machining_mesh_parity.rs` (5 tests). These include: the noise goes; a point 1e-6 off a grid point stays; a collapsed facet is dropped; an inward solid turns outward.\n- `crates/kernel/tests/step_curve_guard.rs` (4 tests).\n- `crates/geometry/tests/mesh_solids.rs` (5 tests).\n- `crates/kernel/tests/machining_mesh.rs` (7 tests, with the changed pins above).\n\n## Readings\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=12): wall 46.8 min, 948 steps, 0 failed, clippy `-D warnings` ok.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main`: wall 64.6 min, 232 steps, 0 failed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The app import still uses the old STEP path. The switch, the app part of the solid ranges and the import tests come in PR B (stacked on this PR).\n- No GUI run.\n\nChangelog: none (no user-visible change until PR B switches the import)\n\nRefs #917\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
